{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Sing, O barren one.</b> The congregation of Israel is a barren one who has not given birth, and she is barren; the meaning is that the number of Israel is small." "<b>Burst forth, even shout.</b> I have explained it." "<b>Did not travail.</b> From the root of חיל <small>(Exodus 15:14)</small>. And so it is: Burst forth, O barren one, in song and shout, who did not travail. And according to the opinion of R. Moses the Cohen, of blessed memory, the Babylonian, and according to the way of truth: every nation that has a husband, and he is a king."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {2 "The phrase ועל דרך האמת introduces Ibn Ezra's own interpretation; the syntax is compressed, juxtaposing the two opinions without a connective. The referent of 'he is a king' is elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:26.110206952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}